 "content": "# Pattern-copy task: isolated 5 markers and a source motif\n\nEvidence: task-4b298da0, one demo and solved test. The grid contains a motif (a connected multicolor arrangement) with a 5 cell within it, plus a separate isolated 5 marking a destination anchor. Copy the motif by translation so that its internal 5 cell aligns with the isolated destination 5. Retain the destination 5 (the copied 5 overlaps it); do not erase or recolor other cells. In the demo, the motif's 5 was at (row 2, col 3) zero-indexed and the isolated destination 5 at (row 7, col 6), so the rest of the motif was copied with offset (+5,+3). In the solved test, the source motif's anchor 5 was isolated at (row 8,col 3), and its destination was the 5 at (row 2,col 6); the copied arrangement used offset (-6,+3). Keep the original motif and markers. Infer the motif and destination from geometry: identify which 5 belongs to/marks the source pattern and which isolated 5 is target; align anchors, then translate all motif cells exactly. The source motif need not be contiguous with its 5 anchor (the test source pattern is nearby/below its isolated 5)."
